# ============================================================================
# HOW TO GET YOUR SUPABASE CREDENTIALS
# ============================================================================

# 1. Go to https://app.supabase.com
# 2. Select your project
# 3. Click "Project Settings" (gear icon, bottom left)
# 4. Select "API" from left menu
# 5. Copy "Project URL" → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
# 6. Copy "anon public" key → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# 7. Save to .env.local

# ============================================================================
# VITE BUILD COMMANDS
# ============================================================================

# Development (with VITE_* prefix, automatically loaded from .env.local):
# npm run dev

# Build with environment file:
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=... VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=... npm run build

# ============================================================================
# SECURITY NOTES
# ============================================================================

# - NEVER commit .env.local to git (add to .gitignore)
# - Never expose service role key in frontend code
# - Anon public key is safe to expose (read-only, rate-limited)
# - Always use environment variables, never hardcode credentials
# - Use Row-Level Security (RLS) policies for data protection
# - Enable Supabase audit logging for compliance

# ============================================================================
# USING IN CODE
# ============================================================================

